WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.570
It's early morning in Kyiv... but there's
already a line-up at the passport office,

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.020
waiting for travel documents.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.980
Anyone who wants to travel to the E-U without
a visa will need a biometric passport.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.600
Olga Antonienko has been here since 7 o'clock.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.480
"Where do I want to go?

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.119
Oh, I've got lots of plans.

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:27.619
My daughter might be going to Belgium next
year to study, and I'd like to visit her."

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:32.840
Negotiations have taken years - the EU had
concerns, including regarding security.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:38.230
But in Strasbourg in mid-May, the last signature
was finally put in place and President Petro

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.879
Poroshenko could celebrate.

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:46.010
But not all Ukrainians will be able to take
advantage of this new freedom of movement.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:52.050
"There are some problems with issuing travel
documents, especially biometric passports,

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:58.039
to the 1.7 million internally displaced people,
and the people living in the occupied zones."

00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:05.110
The EU views this with some concern.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:10.690
Their ambassador in Kyiv wants all agreements
connected with visa liberalization to be correctly fulfilled.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:17.950
"This will not be an easy task because in
some areas now like the fight against corruption,

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:23.689
the rule of law – we know that there are
a number of people in Ukraine who do their

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:27.140
best to backtrack on what has been achieved.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:33.840
And therefore it will be necessary for the
Ukrainian authorities to be extremely vigilant."

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.430
But there are other problems on Olga Antonienko's
mind... the new regulations mean she has to

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:43.560
carry 45 Euros in cash for every day she plans
to spend in the EU.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:48.049
That's a lot of money - for a teacher earning
300 euro a month.

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:51.549
After eight hours waiting, Olga Antonienko
could finally file her application.

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:54.590
In three weeks her new passport will be ready.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.509
"We've waited a long time for this!

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:03.210
Finally we Ukrainians are able to travel out
of the country!"

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:09.000
The Ukrainian foreign ministry also has reason
to celebrate... in their Soviet era headquarters.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.690
The new visa regime was negotiated between
here and Brussels, as part of a much broader

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:16.050
agreement to ease trade barriers.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.310
Now that, too, can come into force...

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:19.310
"Ukraine has passed two milestones on its
journey to Europe.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:20.310
But the party mood is being weighed down by
the ongoing war in the east - and tensions with Russia.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:22.310
The free movement of people between Russia
and Ukraine could soon be restricted.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:22.810
Both Moscow and Kiev are threatening the other
with ending Visa-free travel."

